<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Hydromet year net slips into loss.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Hydromet year net slips into loss.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		loss 5.85 vs profit 5.70</p>
<p>    Net				loss 18.89 vs profit 4.02</p>
<p>    final dividend			  nil vs 1.25</p>
<p>    Sales				    8.24 vs 15.74</p>
<p>    Other income			   0.59 vs 1.48</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		    loss 17.58 vs profit 4.07</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 loss 13.01 vs nil</p>
<p>    Tax					0.03 vs 1.68</p>
<p>    Interest				 0.22 vs 0.11</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   1.35 vs 1.42</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Hydromet Corp Ltd provides hydrometallurgical processing technology to the industrial recycling industry for producing chemical products from industrial residue. It holds a 19.7 percent stake in Canadian Hydromet Environmental Recovery Ltd.</p>
<p>The abnormal loss mainly represented a diminution in the value of investments, a foreign currency loss and the cost of acquiring a controlling interest in Mineral Estates Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
